# What NOT to upload to EAS Build — MONOREPO ROOT copy.
#
# WHY THIS IS HERE AND NOT ONLY IN EACH APP:
# A .easignore was added inside astrowani_customer-main/ first. It had almost no
# effect — the archive went 347 MB -> 339 MB, when excluding android/app/build
# (1.5 GB) and .hot-updater/output (188 MB) should have taken it to single digits.
# That means EAS is building the archive from the GIT REPOSITORY ROOT (this
# directory), not from the app subdirectory, so an ignore file inside the app is
# never consulted. This copy is the one that actually applies.
#
# ⚠️ .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for EAS rather than adding to it, which is why
# obvious entries like node_modules appear below. Omitting them uploads them.
#
# Patterns are matched anywhere in the tree, so a single `node_modules/` covers
# every sub-project.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies — EAS runs a fresh install on the builder.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Native build output. android/app/build alone was 1.5 GB.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
.gradle/
.gradle_cache/
.cxx/
captures/
ios/build/
ios/Pods/
DerivedData/
*.xcworkspace/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# hot-updater OTA output + artifact cache (188 MB of bundle zips and brotli
# blobs). Regenerated on demand; a native build never reads it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
.hot-updater/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sub-projects that are not part of an app binary. The mobile builds do not
# compile the backend, the admin dashboard or the storefront.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
astrowani-backend/
astrowani-admin/
astrowani-shop/
astrowani-store-images/
vps-deployment/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation and scratch — large and irrelevant to a build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
MD files/
docs/
*.md
*.png
*.jpeg
*.jpg
*.pem

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local / editor / OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.expo/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__tests__/
coverage/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-include app assets that the blanket image rules above would otherwise
# strip. These ARE build inputs: launcher icons, the iOS asset catalog and the
# bundled fonts/images the apps ship.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!astrowani_customer-main/android/app/src/main/res/**
!astrowani_customer-main/ios/**/Images.xcassets/**
!astrowani_customer-main/src/assets/**
!astrowani_vendors-main/android/app/src/main/res/**
!astrowani_vendors-main/ios/**/Images.xcassets/**
!astrowani_vendors-main/src/assets/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, so nobody "tidies" them away:
#   */android/app/google-services.json     Firebase config, required
#   */ios/**/GoogleService-Info.plist      Firebase config, required
#   */credentials.json                     eas.json credentialsSource: local
#   */patches/ + */scripts/                run from postinstall
#   */app.json, */eas.json, metro/babel    build inputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
